description[en] = <b>Zulu A7 &mdash; 6 layer, PCBWay, PLAN A (conventional through-hole)</b><p><b>Rebuilt 2026-08-27 on PCBWay's reply</b> to the DFM enquiry of 2026-08-26 (board/PCBWAY-DFM-ENQUIRY.md). What they answered, verbatim: <i>"The bga pad we could build is 8mil and pitch 0.4mm. So your design would be okay for us to handle. And both 0.5 oz and 1oz would work."</i> and <i>"HDI structure would add the manufacturing a lot, so planA would be recommended to use if you want to save the cost."</i><p><b>That retires HDI</b>, which this file used to be built around, and with it the 1+4+1 stackup worry about landing every ball on L2. It also retires the 0.275&nbsp;mm land: at 0.275 the gap between two lands is 0.225&nbsp;mm and NOTHING PCBWay will run on a rigid outer layer fits it &mdash; their finest, 3.5/3.5&nbsp;mil, needs 0.2667. So this variant now uses the same <b>0.225&nbsp;mm land as JLCPCB</b>, which is comfortably above the 8&nbsp;mil (0.2032&nbsp;mm) pad they say they can build, and opens the gap to 0.275&nbsp;mm.<p><b>ONE QUESTION IS STILL OPEN AND IT IS THE ONE THAT MATTERS.</b> They answered the PAD. The binding constraint is the SPACE BETWEEN pads. At 0.500&nbsp;mm pitch, against any land they can build:<p><table><tr><td>land 0.225, gap 0.275</td><td>3.5/3.5 mil needs 0.2667</td><td><b>fits by 0.008</b></td></tr><tr><td></td><td>4/4 mil needs 0.3048</td><td>short by 0.030</td></tr><tr><td>land 0.2032, gap 0.2968</td><td>3.5/3.5 mil</td><td>fits by 0.030</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>4/4 mil</td><td><b>still short by 0.008</b></td></tr></table><p>So 3.5/3.5&nbsp;mil or finer is required <i>whatever the land</i>, and PCBWay's table puts 3.5/3.5 only on the 18&nbsp;um outer-copper row &mdash; while their reply says 0.5&nbsp;oz and 1&nbsp;oz both work, which are heavier. Those two statements are not obviously compatible. <b>The widths below are JLCPCB's numbers pending PCBWay confirming they will run them.</b> Do not order from this file until they do.<p>Stackup unchanged and still their standard through-hole 6-layer 1.6&nbsp;mm, 1&nbsp;oz, 70&nbsp;% residual: 2116 prepreg 0.1195 Dk 4.45 at L1/L2 and L5/L6, 0.430 core Dk 4.60 at L2/L3 and L4/L5, 7628 prepreg 0.1750 Dk 4.74 at L3/L4. They declined to name a 6-layer stackup and pointed at their impedance calculator instead, so this is still read off their published list, not confirmed for this board.<p>An earlier version set 2.5&nbsp;mil on the belief that PCBWay publishes 2/2&nbsp;mil for rigid boards. They do not. Do not restore that number.
